From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:05:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mining_pool(v2): keep coinbase output scripts on the wire

The share-pool coordinator built its coinbase the same way as
BlockAssembler: every output got a single branch, BranchLeaf(script),
next to its legacy scriptPubKey. The coinbase was then serialized in
pure V2 form, which carries only the branch, so every node other than
the one that built the block saw a synthetic 45-byte script instead of
the payout script. A legacy input spending a payout is verified against
the coin's scriptPubKey, so the building node accepted spends that its
peers rejected.

The coordinator now leaves coinbase outputs as it builds them, as
BlockAssembler does after the previous commit. The coinbase is then
serialized in the wrapped V7 form, which carries the scripts. TxId and
TxHash are unchanged, since both come from the V2 view of the outputs.
No test exercises this path directly; the behaviour is the one checked
by miner_tests/coinbase_outputs_survive_wire_round_trip.

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/056)
---
 src/node/mining_pool.cpp | 11 -----------
 1 file changed, 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/node/mining_pool.cpp b/src/node/mining_pool.cpp
index ef7bdd48d5..96395a5998 100644
--- a/src/node/mining_pool.cpp
+++ b/src/node/mining_pool.cpp
@@ -517,17 +517,6 @@ UniValue MiningPoolManager::GetMiningJobJSON(const Config &config,
                                      stakingRewardsPayoutScripts[0]);
     }
 
-    for (auto &out : coinbaseTx.vout) {
-        if (out.vBranches.empty()) {
-            const lotus::v2::Output v2out = out.ToV2Output();
-            out.nFlags = v2out.flags;
-            std::memcpy(out.tokenId.begin(), v2out.token_id.data(), 32);
-            std::memcpy(out.stateRoot.begin(), v2out.state_root.data(), 32);
-            out.vBranches = v2out.branches;
-            out.vPaths = v2out.paths;
-        }
-    }
-
     uint64_t coinbaseSize = ::GetSerializeSize(coinbaseTx);
     if (coinbaseSize < MIN_TX_SIZE) {
         coinbaseTx.vin[0].scriptSig
